{"alias":"/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration","title":"Integrating Instructional Technology","changed":"2026-04-06T22:59:59+00:00","before":"<p>Project Based Learning is one way of implementing interdisciplinary instruction.&nbsp; Below are the steps of Project Based Learning.&nbsp; Each icon is linked to a short video explaining the ideas behind the steps and technologies that can be used with students.&nbsp; If Project Based Learning is new and the idea of doing all of these in one project is overwhelming, start with one step and integrate that into your current teaching.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Click <a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/learning/II/getting-started-ii\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> to learn more about getting started with Interdisciplinary Learning.</p>\r\n<img alt=\"PBL isn't about adding something new to your plate.  It is about rearranging your plate with a focus on student voice and choice. John Spencer\" data-align=\"center\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"a7f98764-00f8-4045-a623-1a61a5cb4f87\" height=\"291\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Powtoon_GIF%20%289%29.gif\" width=\"516\" />\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"d-flex justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/authenticproblems\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Authentic problems\" data-align=\"center\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"16382d03-a15d-4386-b6b0-1abd11428f57\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Authentic%20Problems.png\" width=\"100%\" /></a></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/developingquestions\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Developing Questions\" data-align=\"center\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"503cf665-0ca9-4ec9-816c-f8aa54f85626\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Copy%20of%20Authentic%20Problems.png\" width=\"100%\" /></a></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/researchrefinedesign\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Research, Refine\" data-align=\"center\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"393af03d-ecf5-4d5b-983e-d22cbae4612b\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Research%2C%20Refine%2C%20Design.png\" width=\"100%\" /></a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"d-flex justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/finalartifact\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"final artifact\" data-align=\"center\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"2e35630a-87bc-4335-a7fe-acc713e65463\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Copy%20of%20Reflection%2C%20Feedback%2C%20Assessment.png\" width=\"100%\" /></a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"d-flex justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/showcase\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Showcasing to the public\" data-align=\"center\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"4f193035-f60c-4854-8ee9-e23e55b60439\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Showcasing%20to%20the%20public.png\" width=\"100%\" /></a></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3><strong>Contact</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p paraeid=\"{b4edfa76-4015-45cf-ab3a-0d78f41ceee6}{184}\" paraid=\"803522662\"><strong>Kathy Bertini&nbsp;</strong><br />\r\nInterdisciplinary Instruction Coordinator<br />\r\n<strong>Phone:</strong>&nbsp;(207) 816-0294<br />\r\n<strong>Email</strong>: <a href=\"mailto:kathy.bertini@maine.gov\">Kathy.Bertini@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n","after":"<div class=\"doe-hero\">\n<p class=\"doe-contact-link\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-lead\">Project Based Learning is one way of implementing interdisciplinary instruction. Below are the steps of Project Based Learning. Each icon is linked to a short video explaining the ideas behind the steps and technologies that can be used with students. If Project Based Learning is new and the idea of doing all of these in one project is overwhelming, start with one step and integrate that into your current teaching.</p>\n\n</div>\n\r\n\r\n<p>Click <a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/learning/II/getting-started-ii\">here</a> to learn more about getting started with Interdisciplinary Learning.</p>\r\n<img class=\"doe-img-center\" alt=\"PBL isn't about adding something new to your plate.  It is about rearranging your plate with a focus on student voice and choice. John Spencer\" height=\"291\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Powtoon_GIF%20%289%29.gif\" width=\"516\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"d-flex justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"row\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/authenticproblems\"><img class=\"doe-img-center\" alt=\"Authentic problems\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Authentic%20Problems.png\" width=\"100%\" /></a></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/developingquestions\"><img class=\"doe-img-center\" alt=\"Developing Questions\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/Copy%20of%20Authentic%20Problems.png\" width=\"100%\" /></a></div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-4\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/learning/II/techpblhome/techintegration/researchrefinedesign\"><img cla